5. NON-COMMERCIAL USE / 非商用使用
================================================================
Those who use the Software solely for personal study,
research, education, evaluation, or other non-commercial
purposes are not subject to Section 4 and hold rights
identical to those under the MIT License.

仅为个人学习、研究、教育、评价或其他非商业目的而使用本
软件者，不受第 4 条约束，其权利与 MIT 许可证下完全一致。

================================================================
6. PROPAGATION OF THE LICENSE / 许可证的传递
================================================================
Anyone who distributes the Software (including modified
versions and derivative works) must pass along the full text
of this license. A derivative work may adopt this license or
another license whose terms do not conflict with this license;
however, if its user engages in a Commercial Purpose, the
charity contribution obligation under Section 4 shall still
apply.

任何分发本软件（含修改版、衍生作品）的人，必须一并传递本
许可证全文。衍生作品可自行选择采用本许可证，或采用与本
许可证条款不冲突的其他许可证；但若其使用者欲从事商业用途，
第 4 条慈善回馈义务依然适用。

================================================================
7. INTERPRETATION AND DISPUTES / 解释与争议
================================================================
This license shall be interpreted in a manner consistent with
the freedoms granted in Section 1. If any provision is held
unenforceable in any jurisdiction, such provision shall be
adjusted to the minimum extent necessary, and all remaining
provisions shall remain in full force and effect.

本许可证的解释应以第 1 条授予的自由为原则。各司法管辖区若
认定某条款不可执行，该条款应在最小必要范围内被调整，其余
条款继续完全有效。
